data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Design: Hello App\\n\\nA tiny React application served by Vite that greets the viewer and lets them change the greeting's colour by clicking buttons.\\n\\n## Page structure\\n\\nThe app is wrapped in the `@codesweep-ai/ui` `AppShell` component. Inside the shell:\\n\\n- `Header` at the top with title `\\\"Hello App\\\"`. No logo, no navigation, no actions.\\n- `Footer` at the bottom with the text `\\\"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\\\"` centered.\\n- The main content area uses the `Page` component so the single page scrolls once and centres content on large screens.\\n- Inside `Page`, a `Card` centres the greeting and the button row.\\n\\n## Greeting\\n\\n- Text: `Hello, world!`\\n- The greeting is rendered as a single large, bold heading centred inside the card.\\n- Font size: `var(--font-size-prose-h1)` (2rem / 32px).\\n- Font weight: bold (`var(--font-weight-bold)`).\\n- Text alignment: centre.\\n- Initial colour: `var(--color-info)` (blue).\\n\\n## Colours\\n\\nThe greeting colour changes when the viewer clicks one of four colour buttons. The colours must be taken from the design-system `--color-*` tokens, never from hard-coded hex values.\\n\\n| Button label | Token applied to the greeting |\\n|--------------|------------------------------|\\n| Blue         | `var(--color-info)`          |\\n| Green        | `var(--color-success)`       |\\n| Amber        | `var(--color-warning)`       |\\n| Red          | `var(--color-error)`         |\\n\\n## Buttons\\n\\n- Four `Button` components from `@codesweep-ai/ui` are arranged in a horizontal row, centred below the greeting, with a small gap between them.\\n- Labels are exactly: `Blue`, `Green`, `Amber`, `Red`.\\n- Each button uses the `secondary` variant.\\n- Clicking a button updates the greeting colour to the corresponding token listed above.\\n- The button for the currently active colour should be visually distinguished by using the `primary` variant instead of `secondary`.\\n\\n## State\\n\\n- The active colour is held in React `useState`.\\n- The initial state is the blue/info colour.\\n- State changes are immediate; no async loading or transitions are required.\\n\\n## Styling imports\\n\\nAt the application entry point, import the design-system styles needed for the components used:\\n\\n```js\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/core.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/app-shell.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/button.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/card.css\\\";\\nimport \\\"@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/page.css\\\";\\n```\\n\\n## Layout details\\n\\n- The card is centred both vertically and horizontally in the page content area.\\n- The page content area fills the available viewport height between the header and footer.\\n- Internal spacing inside the card: comfortable padding (`var(--space-6)`), with the greeting above the button row and a gap of `var(--space-4)` between them.\\n- The button row has a gap of `var(--space-2)` between buttons.\\n- No custom CSS should be needed beyond the design-system utilities and component classes; if inline layout is required, use the spacing tokens above.\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- `react` and `react-dom` (Vite defaults are fine).\\n- `@codesweep-ai/ui` at its latest version.\\n- No optional peers (`mermaid`, `puppeteer`, `pixelmatch`, `pngjs`) are needed.\\n- Keep the rest of the dependency list as small as the job allows.\\n\\n## Build and serve commands\\n\\nDocument these in `README.md` at the repository root:\\n\\n- Build: `npm run build`\\n- Serve: `npm run dev` (the dev server must be bound to `0.0.0.0` on port `5173`)\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/hello-app/DESIGN.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_29","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789958881,"id":"chatcmpl-b5debc50af2942efb8c88f76e200c03d","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

